{
  "name": "Boxwood",
  "line": "Every craft at one bench.",
  "voice": {
    "name": "The bench",
    "why": "It speaks as makers rather than as a service, which is what craft first asks for. It carries the name and the studio line without forcing them: boxwood is a maker's wood, and the bench is where every craft meets. It keeps the owner as the author of every decision. Its short, concrete sentences survive a button as well as a home page. The engraver is too terse to explain a choice, the manifesto shouts, and the host and the concierge sound like service, not craft.",
